DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This  is  probably  not the system call that you are interested in; in‐
       stead, see mmmmaapp(2), which describes the glibc wrapper function that in‐
       vokes this system call.

       The mmmmaapp22() system call provides the same interface as mmmmaapp(2),  except
       that the final argument specifies the offset into the file in 4096‐byte
       units (instead of bytes, as is done by mmmmaapp(2)).  This enables applica‐
       tions that use a 32‐bit _o_f_f___t to map large files (up to 2^44 bytes).

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       On success, mmmmaapp22() returns a pointer to the mapped area.  On error, -1
       is returned and _e_r_r_n_o is set to indicate the error.

